> how to use in cmd line

  You can solve the entire challenge directly from the command line using a Python one-liner.

  ### 1. Factor N via curl

  You can retrieve the factors p and q using  curl :

    curl -s "http://factordb.com/api?query=948406957756830799684818171639547165784816468744946013083947881743680617123566349" | jq .factors
    ──────
  ### 2. Decrypt the Flag in One Line

  Once you have the factors, paste this single command into your terminal to compute the private key, decrypt, reverse the bytes, and print the flag:

    python3 -c "
    c = 15341890103764929939105506004034128738090325640037083301857608662849501626260517
    n = 948406957756830799684818171639547165784816468744946013083947881743680617123566349
    e = 65537
    p = 1891771437429478964908181306574287207137
    q = 501332739776173570344039681219489434626477

    d = pow(e, -1, (p - 1) * (q - 1))
    m = pow(c, d, n)
    print(m.to_bytes((m.bit_length() + 7) // 8, 'big')[::-1].decode().strip())
    "

